Projects/UOContent/Engines/Craft/Core/CraftItem.cs, on top of CraftItem-heat-source.patch

Adds one event to CraftItem and raises it wherever the craft system tells the crafter something. Nothing else
changes: every message and every gump is still sent exactly as before, and nothing in the engine subscribes.

ShowCraftMenu is the one place nearly every outcome passes through — twenty call sites: every refusal after
the lock (not near an anvil and a forge, not enough metal, the tool worn out, a strange metal), and the two
endings of an attempt that was made (created, or failed with or without the materials lost). The two exits
above it in Craft do not pass through it, so they are told separately. The hue-aware overload of Craft is
left alone: tailoring's hue path is not one a bot takes.

WHY. The third seam of this kind, after CraftItem.IsHeatSource and HarvestDefinition.Said, and for the second
one's reason exactly. The craft system names every reason an attempt produced nothing. A player reads them. A
bot has no NetState, and neither Mobile.SendLocalizedMessage nor Mobile.SendGump reaches anything without
one, so every sentence was dropped before anything could hear it — and the list of engine rules this project
found by their symptoms is, more than anything else, a list of things crafting refuses without a word:
the action lock, the axe that must be worn, the tool in the hand, the two-material recipe, the fire on the
recipe, the anvil the engine will not accept.

What prompted it: on 20.09.2026 Hale failed at the forge 160 times, "24 attempts, 0 made … nothing came of
the iron", with the iron never running out — so the engine was refusing every attempt before it touched the
metal, and every check the smith makes for itself had passed. Nothing in the code can say which sentence it
was being told. See Projects/BotAIv2/BotCraft/BotCraftEar.cs for the listener, and DECISIONS.md, build 174.

DELIBERATELY NARROW. The event reports what was said and to whom; it cannot alter the message, cannot stop
the send, and a listener that throws is contained so it cannot take the craft with it.

